 ## Overview
-Geometry-Guided Appearance Modeling (GAM) is a method for predicting view-dependent colors in 3D Gaussian Splatting by conditioning the appearance on explicit geometric cues, such as surface normals and learned geometric features derived from a Signed Distance Field (SDF). It solves the limitation of standard Spherical Harmonics (SH), which often fail to capture fine-grained geometric details and high-frequency reflections [S1]. Unlike its sibling [Spherical Harmonics Optimization](14206-spherical-harmonics-optimization.md), which relies on fixed basis functions, GAM replaces or augments SH with a geometry-conditioned Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) [S1].
